The Dow Jones Industrial Average was struggling to advance in early Wednesday trade, with shares of Apple Inc. (AAPL) producing the stiffest headwind for the benchmark stock gauge. The Dow was flat at 25,970, but the index was being weighed by a 1.4%, or $3.21, drop in Apple. That slide would translate to a 22-point toll in the Dow. A $1 swing in any one of the Dow's 30 component equates to a 6.8-point swing in the price-weighted index. Apple is slated to host a product event at 1 p.m. Eastern Time, which will feature upgrades to its roster of consumer products, include the iPhone and the Apple Watch. Meanwhile, the S&P 500 index was off 0.3% at 2,879, while the technology-and-internet laden Nasdaq Composite Index was down 1.1% at 7,887.
-Mark DeCambre;
 1035ET
